1
00:00:02,200 --> 00:00:05,160
THIS SHOW IS CREATED
FOR ENTERTAINMENT PURPOSES ONLY

2
00:00:05,240 --> 00:00:07,520
THE CHARACTERS, BEHAVIORS
AND EVENTS ARE FICTITIOUS

3
00:00:07,600 --> 00:00:09,240
THEY ARE NOT INTENDED TO
DEFAME OR CAUSE DAMAGE

4
00:00:09,320 --> 00:00:10,920
TO ANY ORGANIZATION OR INDIVIDUAL.
VIEWER DISCRETION IS ADVISED.

5
00:02:25,680 --> 00:02:27,040
<i>You make bullets for them, don't you?</i>

6
00:02:37,080 --> 00:02:38,680
Paed, can you hear me? Paed!

7
00:02:39,360 --> 00:02:41,760
Gun, let's go. He's dead.

8
00:02:41,840 --> 00:02:42,720
Go!

9
00:02:44,280 --> 00:02:46,920
<i>Boss, Gun survived.</i>

10
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:50,040
Then I'll have to play my last card.

11
00:03:04,360 --> 00:03:05,960
What about your feelings for me?

12
00:03:09,400 --> 00:03:10,800
Was any of that real?

13
00:03:15,640 --> 00:03:16,880
Answer me.

14
00:03:18,160 --> 00:03:19,400
Answer me.

15
00:03:20,400 --> 00:03:21,760
Was any of that real, Rada?

16
00:03:21,840 --> 00:03:23,160
-Was anything between us--
-Hey!

17
00:03:33,600 --> 00:03:34,600
A GPS tracker.

18
00:03:39,320 --> 00:03:41,000
You sent those guys to Paed.

19
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:47,480
If Seehan sent you to kill me,
why didn't you?

20
00:03:48,160 --> 00:03:50,040
He did send me to kill you,

21
00:03:50,640 --> 00:03:54,200
but Paisan, Decha, and Sirin
were getting too demanding.

22
00:03:54,280 --> 00:03:57,560
He had me keep you alive,
so that you could deal with them.

23
00:03:58,280 --> 00:03:59,600
And once that's done,

24
00:04:01,400 --> 00:04:02,480
you'll kill me?

25
00:04:07,840 --> 00:04:09,120
Finish your mission.

26
00:04:26,040 --> 00:04:27,160
But before I die…

27
00:04:29,160 --> 00:04:30,640
I want to know one thing.

28
00:04:33,480 --> 00:04:34,440
Between us…

29
00:04:38,040 --> 00:04:39,640
Was any of it real to you?

30
00:04:41,400 --> 00:04:43,800
-It doesn't matter to me anymore.
-But it matters to me.

31
00:04:47,600 --> 00:04:49,560
Did you ever really love me?

32
00:04:51,280 --> 00:04:52,640
Or was it all in my head?

33
00:05:03,880 --> 00:05:06,080
Come with me. He wants to capture you.

34
00:05:06,680 --> 00:05:10,200
He doesn't. He wants to kill me
with his own hands.

35
00:05:14,880 --> 00:05:15,960
I trusted you…

36
00:05:20,920 --> 00:05:22,080
because I love you.

37
00:05:28,400 --> 00:05:29,880
So, I'll die by your hand.

38
00:05:41,520 --> 00:05:42,520
Shoot.

39
00:06:10,560 --> 00:06:12,240
Gun, get in!

40
00:06:36,040 --> 00:06:37,480
Miss Rada, you let him get away.

41
00:06:45,160 --> 00:06:47,080
SRIPIAMSUK RESORT
WELCOME

42
00:07:00,560 --> 00:07:01,800
We'll stay here.

43
00:07:02,520 --> 00:07:04,680
Let's regroup, then figure out
our next move.

44
00:07:06,480 --> 00:07:07,440
Sorry

45
00:07:08,880 --> 00:07:09,880
for not believing you.

46
00:07:13,040 --> 00:07:13,880
Forget it.

47
00:07:43,400 --> 00:07:44,840
My dear girl.

48
00:08:16,280 --> 00:08:17,480
I'm sorry

49
00:08:18,400 --> 00:08:20,120
I couldn't bring Gun here.

50
00:08:27,280 --> 00:08:28,400
It's alright, dear.

51
00:08:29,880 --> 00:08:31,800
You've sacrificed enough already,

52
00:08:33,080 --> 00:08:34,520
being with him for so long.

53
00:08:36,360 --> 00:08:39,600
I'll handle the rest myself.

54
00:08:42,360 --> 00:08:43,440
Dad.

55
00:08:45,720 --> 00:08:47,600
Someone attacked Gun

56
00:08:47,680 --> 00:08:51,120
and tried to kill me. Who are they?

57
00:08:51,760 --> 00:08:53,520
Someone dared to do that?

58
00:08:53,600 --> 00:08:54,720
Yes.

59
00:08:57,520 --> 00:08:58,720
Thun.

60
00:08:59,400 --> 00:09:01,040
Do you know who they are?

61
00:09:01,120 --> 00:09:03,280
-They're Madam Sirin's team, sir.
-Hm?

62
00:09:03,920 --> 00:09:05,240
Seriously? Sirin?

63
00:09:07,840 --> 00:09:09,400
She must be so afraid of dying

64
00:09:10,040 --> 00:09:11,200
that she's decided to act.

65
00:09:12,400 --> 00:09:14,920
So, what's next?

66
00:09:16,760 --> 00:09:18,560
End everything.

67
00:09:23,040 --> 00:09:24,200
Kill that bastard Gun.

68
00:09:27,800 --> 00:09:28,720
Yes.

69
00:09:52,960 --> 00:09:56,080
We have to keep moving.
Can't stay in one place.

70
00:10:09,920 --> 00:10:11,240
Nowhere to run, Gun.

71
00:10:15,120 --> 00:10:16,040
Surrender.

72
00:10:16,760 --> 00:10:18,320
Let's fight this with the law.

73
00:10:23,400 --> 00:10:24,640
Confess the truth.

74
00:10:24,720 --> 00:10:26,360
Tell me everything.

75
00:10:26,440 --> 00:10:28,200
I'll use the evidence against him.

76
00:10:29,080 --> 00:10:30,600
You still believe in the system?

77
00:10:32,760 --> 00:10:34,560
I believe if the evidence is solid,

78
00:10:35,160 --> 00:10:36,480
no one can escape.

79
00:10:38,240 --> 00:10:39,560
What evidence do you have?

80
00:10:41,600 --> 00:10:42,960
I'll show you.

81
00:10:43,800 --> 00:10:45,920
-Take them to the car.
-Yes, sir.

82
00:10:53,040 --> 00:10:54,120
-Hey!
-Hey, duck!

83
00:10:54,200 --> 00:10:55,280
Hurry!

84
00:10:56,760 --> 00:10:57,600
Ouch!

85
00:10:57,680 --> 00:10:59,040
Ouch!

86
00:11:11,120 --> 00:11:12,240
Whoa.

87
00:11:18,280 --> 00:11:20,520
-Aut!
-I'm fine.

88
00:11:29,240 --> 00:11:31,760
Choose. Die here

89
00:11:32,400 --> 00:11:33,440
or survive together.

90
00:11:39,160 --> 00:11:40,480
Damn it.

91
00:11:50,160 --> 00:11:51,200
I'm counting on you.

92
00:11:52,240 --> 00:11:53,200
I'll cover you.

93
00:11:54,600 --> 00:11:55,720
Go! Go!

94
00:11:58,360 --> 00:11:59,440
Hurry!

95
00:12:01,080 --> 00:12:02,640
-Methee! Let's go.
-Hurry!

96
00:12:23,840 --> 00:12:25,600
-Ouch.
-Come on.

97
00:12:28,640 --> 00:12:30,520
Let's go. Come here.

98
00:12:31,120 --> 00:12:33,640
-Let go.
-You have to come with me. Go.

99
00:12:35,600 --> 00:12:37,120
I'm going to help Gun. Let go!

100
00:12:38,680 --> 00:12:39,520
Hey!

101
00:12:46,280 --> 00:12:47,640
Stop it! Hey!

102
00:12:53,720 --> 00:12:55,760
Let me go. I'm going to help Gun.

103
00:12:57,360 --> 00:12:58,320
Back off!

104
00:12:59,400 --> 00:13:00,400
You'll come with me.

105
00:13:03,160 --> 00:13:04,040
Handcuff keys.

106
00:13:05,800 --> 00:13:07,160
Now!

107
00:13:51,440 --> 00:13:52,400
Don't shoot.

108
00:13:54,240 --> 00:13:55,480
I'll kill him myself.

109
00:13:58,080 --> 00:13:59,200
Make one move…

110
00:14:02,280 --> 00:14:04,760
and I'll blow his brain out.

111
00:14:08,080 --> 00:14:09,080
Go ahead,

112
00:14:09,880 --> 00:14:11,480
if you want him to die.

113
00:14:19,480 --> 00:14:20,840
You think I care?

114
00:14:42,920 --> 00:14:44,480
Gun, let's go, hurry.

115
00:14:50,000 --> 00:14:50,840
Damn it!

116
00:15:33,680 --> 00:15:35,160
-Boss.
-Oh?

117
00:15:35,800 --> 00:15:37,400
Where is Thun?

118
00:15:37,480 --> 00:15:38,960
Uh, Thun…

119
00:15:42,520 --> 00:15:44,080
He was shot dead by Gun, sir.

120
00:15:45,480 --> 00:15:46,560
Bastard!

121
00:16:13,720 --> 00:16:15,160
How did you survive?

122
00:16:44,120 --> 00:16:45,200
Take off his shirt.

123
00:16:48,520 --> 00:16:49,680
Oh, shit.

124
00:17:12,240 --> 00:17:14,800
Your bulletproof vest saved my life, sir.

125
00:17:31,920 --> 00:17:33,880
I raised you…

126
00:17:36,880 --> 00:17:37,880
for this day.

127
00:17:39,600 --> 00:17:41,400
Go finish it.

128
00:17:43,000 --> 00:17:45,400
Before I have no one left to work for me.

129
00:17:49,880 --> 00:17:51,320
Yes, Dad.

130
00:20:04,800 --> 00:20:06,200
How do you know when it's coming?

131
00:20:11,960 --> 00:20:14,000
I have superpowers.

132
00:20:17,440 --> 00:20:19,480
Well, the window glass
always shakes first.

133
00:20:22,560 --> 00:20:24,760
I'm sorry. I forgot.

134
00:20:44,680 --> 00:20:45,920
You really like watching it?

135
00:20:51,760 --> 00:20:53,600
I like it when it passes by.

136
00:20:55,880 --> 00:20:59,160
It feels like my thoughts and dreams

137
00:20:59,240 --> 00:21:00,560
are rushing along with it.

138
00:21:01,080 --> 00:21:02,760
What is your dream?

139
00:21:05,000 --> 00:21:06,920
I don't have any big dreams.

140
00:21:07,800 --> 00:21:10,720
I just want to live a quiet life
in the countryside

141
00:21:11,400 --> 00:21:13,360
with someone

142
00:21:13,440 --> 00:21:15,160
I can share meals with.

143
00:21:17,160 --> 00:21:18,320
That's it?

144
00:21:21,000 --> 00:21:22,280
Other women

145
00:21:23,520 --> 00:21:25,280
might dream of a big house

146
00:21:26,520 --> 00:21:28,240
and a loving family.

147
00:21:30,440 --> 00:21:32,400
For someone like me, who grew up

148
00:21:33,920 --> 00:21:36,600
in an orphanage

149
00:21:37,880 --> 00:21:39,880
without a father or a mother,

150
00:21:41,600 --> 00:21:44,360
this is more than enough.

151
00:21:47,200 --> 00:21:48,560
That's all my dream is.

152
00:21:57,600 --> 00:21:59,320
Why did you

153
00:21:59,400 --> 00:22:02,840
quit the force to become a hitman?

154
00:22:17,960 --> 00:22:20,040
Scammers are expanding
their reach right now,

155
00:22:21,400 --> 00:22:22,840
conning the whole country.

156
00:22:24,200 --> 00:22:26,080
Many have lost millions.

157
00:22:26,680 --> 00:22:28,480
Some have lost all they had.

158
00:22:28,560 --> 00:22:30,080
Some took their own lives.

159
00:22:33,640 --> 00:22:35,280
I couldn't just stand by.

160
00:22:39,360 --> 00:22:41,640
I'm not killing to avenge my grandma.

161
00:22:44,320 --> 00:22:45,680
I just need to stop them.

162
00:22:48,200 --> 00:22:50,360
When the law can't do anything,

163
00:22:52,720 --> 00:22:54,040
death

164
00:22:55,480 --> 00:22:56,480
is the only answer.

165
00:24:00,760 --> 00:24:01,720
Hey.

166
00:24:04,600 --> 00:24:05,720
Why are we stopping?

167
00:24:05,800 --> 00:24:07,240
We haven't gone far.

168
00:24:08,120 --> 00:24:09,400
You go.

169
00:24:11,200 --> 00:24:13,160
You've suffered enough because of me.

170
00:24:17,120 --> 00:24:18,480
How are you going to fight him?

171
00:24:19,280 --> 00:24:20,480
You have no bullets

172
00:24:21,240 --> 00:24:23,160
and no way to get to Seehan.

173
00:24:23,240 --> 00:24:24,640
Rada can help me.

174
00:24:27,560 --> 00:24:28,600
Damn it.

175
00:24:30,000 --> 00:24:31,520
You're about to die

176
00:24:32,400 --> 00:24:34,480
and you still trust
that treacherous woman?

177
00:24:35,120 --> 00:24:36,400
But she's the one

178
00:24:37,920 --> 00:24:39,880
closest to Seehan.

179
00:24:39,960 --> 00:24:41,520
Did you forget

180
00:24:42,080 --> 00:24:43,520
he's her adopted father?

181
00:24:44,520 --> 00:24:47,400
Everything you see could be a setup.

182
00:24:47,480 --> 00:24:49,360
I know she played me,

183
00:24:51,240 --> 00:24:53,120
but deep down,

184
00:24:53,840 --> 00:24:55,560
I know Rada isn't like that.

185
00:24:58,960 --> 00:25:00,880
I caused this mess,

186
00:25:00,960 --> 00:25:02,480
and I'll take responsibility.

187
00:25:03,560 --> 00:25:05,600
You don't have to risk your life for me.

188
00:25:13,000 --> 00:25:14,160
I'm not leaving.

189
00:25:21,920 --> 00:25:23,320
You're my friend.

190
00:25:24,440 --> 00:25:26,720
Whatever you do, I'm in.

191
00:25:50,680 --> 00:25:51,560
Here.

192
00:26:05,560 --> 00:26:06,600
What is it, dear?

193
00:26:09,800 --> 00:26:10,680
Dad,

194
00:26:11,800 --> 00:26:13,280
did you ever have a dream?

195
00:26:16,640 --> 00:26:19,720
I'm too old to have childhood dreams.

196
00:26:20,640 --> 00:26:21,680
Why do you ask?

197
00:26:25,760 --> 00:26:28,520
As long as we're alive,

198
00:26:29,920 --> 00:26:31,960
there must be something
we truly want to do.

199
00:26:35,120 --> 00:26:36,720
You have everything,

200
00:26:37,640 --> 00:26:40,320
businesses, money,

201
00:26:41,080 --> 00:26:42,400
and respect.

202
00:26:45,720 --> 00:26:46,640
Can't you…

203
00:26:48,960 --> 00:26:51,000
stop the scammer business?

204
00:26:53,560 --> 00:26:55,040
What did Gun tell you?

205
00:26:57,440 --> 00:26:59,120
No one brainwashed me.

206
00:27:00,600 --> 00:27:02,120
I just feel

207
00:27:03,120 --> 00:27:04,240
that money

208
00:27:05,320 --> 00:27:06,760
comes at the cost of people's lives.

209
00:27:10,080 --> 00:27:11,960
Every time I hear about the victims,

210
00:27:13,480 --> 00:27:14,960
about people suffering

211
00:27:15,960 --> 00:27:17,280
and taking their own lives…

212
00:27:19,840 --> 00:27:20,840
I'm

213
00:27:21,600 --> 00:27:22,840
not happy at all.

214
00:27:24,040 --> 00:27:25,720
Let me tell you something.

215
00:27:27,640 --> 00:27:30,760
Our country isn't as pure as you think.

216
00:27:45,320 --> 00:27:46,400
And most importantly,

217
00:27:46,920 --> 00:27:48,840
I love you very much. You know that?

218
00:27:51,440 --> 00:27:53,080
Everything I do,

219
00:27:53,160 --> 00:27:55,520
everything I've built,

220
00:27:56,240 --> 00:27:57,880
will eventually be yours.

221
00:28:01,520 --> 00:28:02,400
If

222
00:28:03,560 --> 00:28:05,360
you really love me,

223
00:28:07,080 --> 00:28:08,120
can you

224
00:28:09,280 --> 00:28:11,000
stop this?

225
00:28:14,240 --> 00:28:15,560
Of course.

226
00:28:20,560 --> 00:28:22,360
I'll give it all up…

227
00:28:26,280 --> 00:28:28,680
but you have to kill Gun.

228
00:28:38,640 --> 00:28:40,240
I promise you,

229
00:28:41,720 --> 00:28:44,240
I'm willing to give up everything…

230
00:28:46,960 --> 00:28:49,720
and do whatever you want…

231
00:28:53,880 --> 00:28:55,720
but you must kill him.

232
00:29:01,560 --> 00:29:03,280
Yes, Dad.

233
00:29:11,520 --> 00:29:15,640
BAAN TON OR ORPHANAGE

234
00:29:18,200 --> 00:29:19,520
Thank you very much, Teacher.

235
00:29:19,600 --> 00:29:22,480
You're welcome. If there's
anything else, I'll contact you.

236
00:29:22,560 --> 00:29:23,800
Yes.

237
00:29:23,880 --> 00:29:26,280
-Wela, come here.
-Yes, Teacher.

238
00:29:39,320 --> 00:29:41,080
Well? Found anything?

239
00:29:44,400 --> 00:29:46,160
After Rada's parents died,

240
00:29:46,720 --> 00:29:47,920
she was brought here.

241
00:29:48,560 --> 00:29:50,600
And Seehan really did adopt her.

242
00:29:54,160 --> 00:29:55,280
Just like she said.

243
00:29:58,640 --> 00:29:59,920
But I feel like

244
00:30:01,160 --> 00:30:02,760
there's more to it.

245
00:30:05,720 --> 00:30:10,040
Where are you digging next?
The district office? Civil registration?

246
00:30:12,280 --> 00:30:15,920
I want to know whether Seehan
simply adopted her

247
00:30:17,200 --> 00:30:18,600
or had singled her out beforehand.

248
00:30:24,880 --> 00:30:26,600
Are you hurt, sweetie?

249
00:30:26,680 --> 00:30:27,640
No.

250
00:30:28,160 --> 00:30:29,200
Be careful.

251
00:30:59,040 --> 00:30:59,880
What is it?

252
00:31:04,960 --> 00:31:06,960
Gun wants detailed information about Rada.

253
00:31:07,960 --> 00:31:10,480
You're helping Gun anyway.
I shouldn't have asked.

254
00:31:12,640 --> 00:31:14,400
It might not just be helping him.

255
00:31:15,200 --> 00:31:16,440
How so?

256
00:31:16,520 --> 00:31:20,520
Someone like Seehan wouldn't
take in an orphan for nothing.

257
00:31:21,360 --> 00:31:22,360
There has to be a reason.

258
00:31:25,120 --> 00:31:27,560
Maybe Rada wasn't just adopted.

259
00:31:28,640 --> 00:31:30,080
Find out everything about her.

260
00:31:30,680 --> 00:31:32,560
Starting from the day her parents died.

261
00:31:32,640 --> 00:31:34,560
I want to know how Seehan found her.

262
00:31:35,680 --> 00:31:36,600
Yes, sir.

263
00:32:06,800 --> 00:32:07,920
How many days has it been?

264
00:32:08,920 --> 00:32:11,680
You should stop relying on Sarawut.

265
00:32:17,760 --> 00:32:19,320
He'll just preach to you again.

266
00:32:22,840 --> 00:32:25,600
"Fight with the law. Use evidence."

267
00:32:31,920 --> 00:32:33,200
He sent it.

268
00:32:37,440 --> 00:32:40,000
Damn. He really helped.

269
00:32:49,360 --> 00:32:50,280
What is it?

270
00:32:52,800 --> 00:32:53,960
Her father was a cop.

271
00:32:55,000 --> 00:32:56,520
And he didn't die in an accident.

272
00:32:59,800 --> 00:33:01,440
Didn't die in an accident?

273
00:33:03,600 --> 00:33:04,480
But

274
00:33:04,560 --> 00:33:05,760
what does that mean?

275
00:33:07,320 --> 00:33:09,000
They ruled it an accident,

276
00:33:10,480 --> 00:33:11,840
but it was actually murder.

277
00:33:45,960 --> 00:33:47,200
<i>I need to talk to you.</i>

278
00:33:48,640 --> 00:33:50,000
<i>I'll send you the location.</i>

279
00:34:34,159 --> 00:34:35,560
Where are you going, dear?

280
00:34:36,440 --> 00:34:37,400
To work.

281
00:34:38,520 --> 00:34:40,320
You found Gun's hideout?

282
00:34:42,040 --> 00:34:42,960
Not yet.

283
00:34:44,000 --> 00:34:46,320
But I know where to start looking.

284
00:34:48,040 --> 00:34:51,080
Then I'll have Thun go with you.

285
00:34:51,159 --> 00:34:52,679
It's fine.

286
00:34:52,760 --> 00:34:54,679
It's easier to move alone.

287
00:34:56,199 --> 00:34:57,600
I worry about you.

288
00:35:03,280 --> 00:35:04,520
Don't worry, Dad.

289
00:35:05,680 --> 00:35:07,720
I know Gun won't kill me.

290
00:35:12,160 --> 00:35:13,560
He seems to love you so much.

291
00:35:16,760 --> 00:35:17,800
What about you?

292
00:35:20,800 --> 00:35:22,000
Do you love him?

293
00:35:26,520 --> 00:35:27,960
You always taught me

294
00:35:28,880 --> 00:35:30,440
never to love the enemy.

295
00:35:45,920 --> 00:35:47,240
Why did you ask me to meet?

296
00:35:52,440 --> 00:35:54,000
I investigated your parents.

297
00:35:59,800 --> 00:36:01,400
They didn't die in an accident.

298
00:36:06,880 --> 00:36:07,920
They were murdered.

299
00:36:11,040 --> 00:36:12,160
And everything…

300
00:36:14,560 --> 00:36:15,800
points to Seehan.

301
00:36:20,880 --> 00:36:21,840
That's not true.

302
00:36:28,000 --> 00:36:29,080
Rada.

303
00:36:32,040 --> 00:36:34,080
I didn't come here to hurt you.

304
00:36:37,200 --> 00:36:39,520
I don't want to see you
used by him anymore.

305
00:36:45,520 --> 00:36:47,160
I never feared death before.

306
00:36:50,800 --> 00:36:52,200
But after meeting you…

307
00:36:58,800 --> 00:37:00,480
you changed my heart.

308
00:37:03,720 --> 00:37:05,200
Even though I deceived you,

309
00:37:06,920 --> 00:37:08,400
you still agreed to meet me.

310
00:37:12,320 --> 00:37:13,600
I want you to know.

311
00:37:16,240 --> 00:37:17,840
No matter what happens,

312
00:37:19,400 --> 00:37:20,440
I still love you.

313
00:37:28,960 --> 00:37:30,160
Do you love me?

314
00:37:31,960 --> 00:37:33,360
I love you very much.

315
00:37:40,800 --> 00:37:43,720
I won't let anyone kill you.

316
00:37:50,360 --> 00:37:51,920
<i>I promise you,</i>

317
00:37:54,160 --> 00:37:56,760
<i>I'm willing to give up everything.</i>

318
00:38:01,040 --> 00:38:03,320
<i>But you must kill him.</i>

319
00:38:40,800 --> 00:38:41,880
Gun.

320
00:38:42,680 --> 00:38:43,520
Gun.

321
00:38:45,880 --> 00:38:47,040
<i>My friend just died.</i>

322
00:38:47,720 --> 00:38:49,560
You think I'm in the mood for jokes?

323
00:38:52,240 --> 00:38:55,000
<i>Don't worry. Your soul won't be lonely.</i>

324
00:38:55,080 --> 00:38:57,160
<i>Your friend will be joining you soon.</i>

325
00:39:12,120 --> 00:39:15,160
<i>And… action!</i>

326
00:39:16,160 --> 00:39:17,480
-Hey!
-Hey, duck!

327
00:39:21,200 --> 00:39:24,160
<i>Moo, come out and shoot.</i>
<i>Buddy, enter, then exit!</i>

328
00:39:25,080 --> 00:39:26,040
-<i>Good.</i>
-Ouch!

329
00:39:26,560 --> 00:39:28,240
<i>Step back.</i>

330
00:39:28,320 --> 00:39:29,520
<i>Quick.</i>

331
00:39:29,600 --> 00:39:32,000
<i>I told you not to shoot.</i>

332
00:39:32,680 --> 00:39:33,600
Try it.

333
00:39:34,840 --> 00:39:36,080
You okay?

334
00:39:36,160 --> 00:39:37,520
Today went well.

335
00:39:37,600 --> 00:39:39,320
They didn't hurt me.

336
00:39:40,160 --> 00:39:43,880
<i>From where they talk and then take cover.</i>

337
00:39:43,960 --> 00:39:44,840
<i>Okay?</i>

338
00:39:44,920 --> 00:39:47,760
<i>For the second one, start from…</i>

339
00:39:48,400 --> 00:39:49,960
Come on! Up!

340
00:39:50,040 --> 00:39:51,760
-Methee! Let's go.
-Hurry!

341
00:39:59,360 --> 00:40:00,320
Oh, let me uncuff you.

342
00:40:02,400 --> 00:40:03,560
So much blood.

343
00:40:03,640 --> 00:40:05,000
-Loved it.
-Did you like it?

344
00:40:05,080 --> 00:40:07,120
Damn, blood on this hand,
but you used the other?

345
00:40:07,200 --> 00:40:08,720
Gosh, that was a trick.

346
00:40:09,840 --> 00:40:10,680
Oh, Ben.

347
00:40:11,440 --> 00:40:13,160
<i>Stand in for me. Hold still, okay?</i>

348
00:40:13,240 --> 00:40:15,520
-<i>Camera B, wider shot.</i>
-We're all moved here.

349
00:40:15,600 --> 00:40:18,160
-Ready in front, ready.
-No, stay there and change the pose.

350
00:40:18,240 --> 00:40:19,200
Alright.

351
00:40:20,560 --> 00:40:22,080
Are the gun barrels in the shot?

352
00:40:24,720 --> 00:40:26,560
Ready. Bring in the slate.

353
00:40:26,640 --> 00:40:27,920
Check.

354
00:40:31,680 --> 00:40:34,160
-Cut 12, take two.
-Wait.

355
00:40:35,920 --> 00:40:37,320
Go.

356
00:40:37,400 --> 00:40:38,760
<i>Mik, my advice.</i>

357
00:40:38,840 --> 00:40:42,440
<i>Your hands don't have to line up.</i>
<i>Looks cooler if they're slightly offset.</i>

358
00:40:42,520 --> 00:40:45,120
-Got it.
-<i>Ready? Camera. And…</i>

359
00:40:46,360 --> 00:40:47,400
<i>action!</i>

360
00:40:51,760 --> 00:40:53,680
<i>That was it? Okay!</i>

361
00:40:53,760 --> 00:40:57,160
-<i>Pass. You guys can go rest.</i>
-Cut.

362
00:40:57,240 --> 00:40:59,320
We just discussed not moving anymore.

363
00:40:59,400 --> 00:41:00,760
Okay, understood.

364
00:41:03,040 --> 00:41:04,160
Alright.

365
00:41:04,240 --> 00:41:06,360
Surrender. Let's fight this with the law.

366
00:41:47,120 --> 00:41:48,640
Subtitle translation by: Anan Pratchayakul
